# Rank 1376 / CVE-2025-53370 (GHSA-prmv-7r8c-794g, CWE-79):
# StarCitizenTools/mediawiki-skins-Citizen is a MediaWiki skin. Its page-heading
# component builds the string the skin renders under the page title -- the
# "tagline" -- and prefers a short description supplied by Extension:ShortDescription
# or by Wikibase over its own computed one:
#
#   private function getTagline(): string {
#     $shortdesc = $this->out->getProperty( 'shortdesc' );
#     if ( $shortdesc ) {
#       $tagline = $shortdesc;
#     } else {
#       $tagline = $this->determineTagline();
#     }
#     if ( $tagline !== '' ) { $tagline = $langConv->convert( $tagline ); }
#     return $tagline;
#   }
#
#   public function getTemplateData(): array {
#     return [ 'html-tagline' => $this->getTagline(), ... ];
#   }
#
# The weakness, stated from the diff rather than the advisory: `getTagline()` mixes
# two kinds of string into one variable and then hands the result to a template key
# that is by convention raw HTML. The `else` branch is markup on purpose --
# `determineTagline()` returns `Html::rawElement(...)` output or a parsed interface
# message -- so `html-tagline` is consumed unescaped:
# templates/PageHeading.mustache renders it as `{{{html-tagline}}}`. The `if` branch
# is not markup: `OutputPage::getProperty( 'shortdesc' )` returns a page property an
# extension set from the page's own wikitext, so it is text any user who can edit a
# page (or an item on a connected Wikibase repository) controls. Assigning it into
# the same raw-HTML slot stores attacker markup in every page view. Two branches
# feed one variable, one of them is trusted to be HTML and the other is not, and the
# variable's consumer trusts both.
#
# c85a40bddc8651fff66df83a72debddcb34f0521 escapes exactly the untrusted branch and
# leaves the markup branch alone:
#
#   -   $tagline = $shortdesc;
#   +   $tagline = htmlspecialchars( $shortdesc, ENT_QUOTES );
#
# The row is correct: repository and commit both check out, and the single-line change above is
# the whole fix. The vulnerable construct is present at the parent, c85a40bddc^,
# at includes/Components/CitizenComponentPageHeading.php:251. The recorded CWE-79
# is right. No corpus correction.
#
# The vulnerable file is PHP. A skin also ships client JavaScript and Mustache
# templates, and both matter here: findings land in source, since the repository
# commits no built assets (`resources/` is ResourceLoader source, bundled at request
# time), but the raw-HTML boundary this weakness crosses is in
# templates/PageHeading.mustache -- and `.mustache` matches no frontend at all. A
# bounded scan of the vulnerable checkout reports `908 file(s) matched no frontend`,
# 45 of them `.mustache`. PHP alternative-syntax view code (the `colon_block` gap
# from rank 1328) is *not* a factor: Citizen's views are Mustache, and its PHP
# contains no `if (...):`/`endif` bodies at all.
#
# What fires today, union over three `timeout 180 ./bin/vyql scan --cache off
# --max-ram 6GB` runs of the vulnerable checkout (identical all three, so the
# nondeterminism band is not in play): 7 findings and 2 flags, none of them about
# the tagline. Four are in .github/workflows/installWiki.sh (2x VYQL-PATH-001,
# 2x VYQL-RF-001, all from a bash source), one is VYQL-DOS-001 on a regex built
# from DOM input in resources/skins.citizen.scripts/inline.js:19, and the last two
# are the flag pair: VYQL-INJ-134 / code.NestedPathInheritedPropertyPrototypePollution
# on resources/skins.citizen.search/searchClients/mwActionApi.js:85 and VYQL-INJ-115 /
# code.UnsanitizedSvgUpload on includes/Api/ApiWebappManifest.php:43. `vyql match`
# on the vulnerable file lists eleven sinks (five `Html::rawElement` argument
# positions in the *user* tagline builders, one `preg_replace`) and, decisively,
# `== source == (none)`: the page-property read is unlabelled.
#
# Vocabulary is checked for reuse before anything is written, and nothing needs
# minting. code.HtmlRender carries CWE-79 with excludedChars "<>\"'";
# core.HtmlEscape binds `htmlspecialchars` and neutralises
# injection.Xss, so VYQL-INJ-004 (`core.UserControlledData -> code.HtmlRender unless
# path coveredBy core.HtmlEscape`) is exactly the rule this fix satisfies. For the
# no-taint-path route, code.StoredHtmlWrite is the existing review concept whose
# `expected: [core.HtmlEscape]` and reviewCondition ("stored HTML is written without
# a proven sanitizer before later rendering") describe this weakness verbatim. No
# rule ID and no concept is minted here; the two cases below that pin the review
# concept use code.StoredHtmlWrite, and the two that pin the taint miss use
# VYQL-INJ-004.
#
# ATTENTION, engine gap. Two independent blockers, both measured.
#
# Blocker 1 -- there is no node the raw-HTML sink can attach to. The value becomes
# HTML at `{{{html-tagline}}}` in a Mustache template, and the PHP-side handoff is
# an array-literal entry, `'html-tagline' => $this->getTagline()`. `vyql graph` over
# the vulnerable file shows what survives lowering for that array: one
# `Seq path=__object_literal` and one `CollectionElement vkind=Seq` per entry,
# holding the entry *values* only. The key text is nowhere in the USG, so the one
# fact that says "this slot is raw HTML" -- MediaWiki's documented skin convention
# that template-data keys prefixed `html-` are inserted unescaped -- is unreadable.
# And a sink can only be emitted from a `callExpr` binding: across all 30810
# bindings in the tree, 29078 use `callExpr` and 1732 use `presenceNode`, and every
# one of the latter emits `issue` (1720), `check` (7) or `source` (1) -- never
# `sink`. There is no call at the boundary, so there is no position to bind. The
# whole XSS taint apparatus therefore cannot reach this fix even though every other
# piece of it is present and correct.
#
# Blocker 2 -- interprocedural return flow through `$this->method()` in PHP is
# resolved by method name across the whole program, so a same-named method on any
# other class silences it. This is separable from blocker 1 and is what the second
# pair below pins. Cases 3 and 4 are one file each, differing in exactly one token:
# the *sibling* class's method is named `getTagline` in case 3 and `getFooter` in
# case 4. Case 4 reports VYQL-INJ-004; case 3 reports nothing, and
# `vyql trace -from code.HttpInput -to code.HtmlRender` on it says
# `taint stops at ... call=analysis.function.return -- no outgoing flow (callee not
# traced -- external or cross-package)`. Replacing `$this->getTagline()` with
# `self::getTagline()` in case 3, changing nothing else, restores the finding, which
# localises the defect to the `$this` receiver rather than to the collision.
#
# The cause is a receiver-name mismatch in
# internal/extract/lowering/lowering.go. `resolveCalleeInfos`' `nir.Attr` arm takes
# `obj := base.ID`, which for PHP is the literal text `$this`, and looks up
# `sc.typ[obj]` to find the receiver's class. The scope's self entry is keyed
# `this`, without the sigil: the PHP frontend declares `nir.Program{SelfName:
# "this"}` (php.go:42), and both places that seed a self type -- `inner.setTyp(
# l.selfName, ...)` at lowering.go:3028, gated on the method declaring self as its
# first parameter, which PHP methods do not, and the C#-only implicit-`this` block
# at 3037-3041, gated on `ClassDef.Members` being populated, which the PHP frontend
# never does -- leave it unset for PHP either way. The `obj == "super"` case two
# lines above is handled explicitly; `$this` is the missing sibling. With the
# receiver class unknown, resolution falls through to the cross-file fallback at
# lowering.go:5112, `l.uniqueTechFuncInfo(l.funcShort[c.Attr])`, which by design
# refuses to resolve when two tech-compatible definitions share the short name
# (lowering.go:5152, "ambiguous -- second compatible match"). Citizen declares
# `getTemplateData()` on seventeen classes, so even with blocker 1 removed no path
# out of a skin component would survive. This is *not* recorded as mechanical: the
# repair needs the frontend to declare or synthesize a typed self for PHP, not a
# single missing case, and it changes which body every `$this->m()` in every PHP
# scan routes through -- routing through a concrete body also starts honouring
# in-body sanitizers, so it can delete findings as well as add them, which is the
# bidirectional hazard rank 1346's `sameReceiver` measurement and the rejected
# declared-type-chain change both ran into.
#
# What is measured, so the next session does not re-derive it. Both
# variants below emit an existing review concept from a throwaway PHP binding,
# scored with `-flags only` against both revisions of the real repository.
#
# 1. Function-confined, keyed on the property read:
#      node.scope == "function" and node.context.language == "php"
#      and node.context.assignCallMethod contains "getProperty"
#      and not (containsAny(node.context.assignCallMethod,
#          ["htmlspecialchars", "htmlentities", "escapeHtml", "strip_tags", "esc_html"]))
#    discriminates perfectly -- 1 flag on the vulnerable revision, at
#    CitizenComponentPageHeading.php:246, and 0 on the fixed one -- and the clause is
#    genuinely function-confined, because `assign_call_method:` is absent from
#    flagASTRoutingValuePrefixes (internal/bindings/bindings_match.go:730) so it stays
#    on the node's own `str_args`. It is still not shippable. Its entire
#    discriminating power is that `getProperty` happens to be assigned exactly once
#    in this repository: the clause says nothing about the value being rendered as
#    HTML, which is the review concept's stated assumption, and `getProperty` is an
#    ordinary getter name. Nobody reading MediaWiki's documentation would write it,
#    which is the genericity test in AGENTS.md, and the next variant of this weakness
#    -- a short description arriving from a hook or from `ParserOutput` rather than
#    from `getProperty` -- walks straight past it.
#
# 2. The honest generalisation, anchored on the raw-HTML key instead of the getter,
#    at class scope because the key and the read are in different methods:
#      node.scope == "class" and node.context.language == "php"
#      and node.context.literal contains "html-"
#      and not (containsAny(node.context.assignCallMethod, [<the same escapers>]))
#    reports 7 flags on the vulnerable revision and 6 on the fixed one: 1 true and 6
#    false on the repository the CVE is in, the false ones being
#    CitizenComponentLink.php:14, CitizenComponentMenu.php:12,
#    CitizenComponentSearchBox.php:14, SkinCitizen.php:47 and two test fixtures,
#    CitizenComponentLinkTest.php:17 and CitizenComponentMenuTest.php:15 -- every
#    component that legitimately assembles markup with `Html::rawElement` before
#    putting it in an `html-` key, which is the correct use of the convention. 1-in-7
#    on the vulnerable tree is the shape ranks 1311, 1331 and 1343 measure
#    unshippable. Class scope is also the co-membership trap from the rejected
#    whole-file computations: with one class per file it is file scope, and
#    `literal:` routes through the AST path file-wide regardless.
#
# Behaviour a shippable fact needs, in order of how much it unblocks:
#  a. Array/object-literal *keys* represented in the USG, and a binding position
#     that can attach a sink to a literal entry's value. Then MediaWiki's `html-`
#     prefix convention becomes one ordinary PHP sink binding emitting
#     code.HtmlRender, and VYQL-INJ-004 covers this class of skin and extension
#     stored XSS with no new concept and no new rule. This is the general form of a
#     gap that any template-data-array framework hits, not a MediaWiki one.
#  b. A typed self for PHP so `$this->m()` resolves through its own class
#     (blocker 2 above), without which (a) alone still yields nothing on a real
#     skin.
#
# The four cases below are the two minimal pairs. Cases 1 and 2 are the real
# vulnerable and patched `getTagline()`, both rejected today, pinning the review
# miss. Cases 3 and 4 differ only in the sibling class's method name and isolate the
# `$this` resolution gap.
#
# verify_current_expected: attention-engine-gap; cases 1-3 rejected, case 4 expected.

test "rank1376: a skin page-heading component assigns an extension-supplied short description into the raw-HTML tagline key"
  lang php
  file includes/Components/CitizenComponentPageHeading.php
  reject_review code.StoredHtmlWrite
  code
  ```
  <?php

  declare( strict_types=1 );

  namespace MediaWiki\Skins\Citizen\Components;

  use MediaWiki\Html\Html;
  use MediaWiki\MediaWikiServices;
  use MediaWiki\Output\OutputPage;
  use MessageLocalizer;

  class CitizenComponentPageHeading {

  	public function __construct(
  		private MediaWikiServices $services,
  		private MessageLocalizer $localizer,
  		private OutputPage $out,
  		private string $titleData
  	) {
  	}

  	private function getCitizenTagline( string $msgKey ): string {
  		$msg = $this->localizer->msg( $msgKey );
  		if ( $msg->isDisabled() ) {
  			$msg = $this->localizer->msg( 'tagline' );
  		}
  		return $msg->parse();
  	}

  	private function determineTagline(): string {
  		return Html::rawElement(
  			'div',
  			[ 'id' => 'citizen-tagline-user' ],
  			$this->getCitizenTagline( 'citizen-tagline' )
  		);
  	}

  	/**
  	 * Return the page tagline based on the current page
  	 */
  	private function getTagline(): string {
  		// Use short description if there is any
  		// from Extension:ShortDescription
  		$shortdesc = $this->out->getProperty( 'shortdesc' );
  		if ( $shortdesc ) {
  			$tagline = $shortdesc;
  		} else {
  			$tagline = $this->determineTagline();
  		}

  		if ( $tagline !== '' ) {
  			// Apply language variant conversion
  			$langConv = $this->services
  				->getLanguageConverterFactory()
  				->getLanguageConverter( $this->services->getContentLanguage() );
  			$tagline = $langConv->convert( $tagline );
  		}

  		return $tagline;
  	}

  	/**
  	 * @inheritDoc
  	 */
  	public function getTemplateData(): array {
  		return [
  			'html-tagline' => $this->getTagline(),
  			'html-title-heading' => $this->titleData
  		];
  	}
  }
  ```

test "rank1376: the same component escaping the short description before it reaches the raw-HTML tagline key"
  lang php
  file includes/Components/CitizenComponentPageHeading.php
  reject_review code.StoredHtmlWrite
  code
  ```
  <?php

  declare( strict_types=1 );

  namespace MediaWiki\Skins\Citizen\Components;

  use MediaWiki\Html\Html;
  use MediaWiki\MediaWikiServices;
  use MediaWiki\Output\OutputPage;
  use MessageLocalizer;

  class CitizenComponentPageHeading {

  	public function __construct(
  		private MediaWikiServices $services,
  		private MessageLocalizer $localizer,
  		private OutputPage $out,
  		private string $titleData
  	) {
  	}

  	private function getCitizenTagline( string $msgKey ): string {
  		$msg = $this->localizer->msg( $msgKey );
  		if ( $msg->isDisabled() ) {
  			$msg = $this->localizer->msg( 'tagline' );
  		}
  		return $msg->parse();
  	}

  	private function determineTagline(): string {
  		return Html::rawElement(
  			'div',
  			[ 'id' => 'citizen-tagline-user' ],
  			$this->getCitizenTagline( 'citizen-tagline' )
  		);
  	}

  	/**
  	 * Return the page tagline based on the current page
  	 */
  	private function getTagline(): string {
  		// Use short description if there is any
  		// from Extension:ShortDescription
  		$shortdesc = $this->out->getProperty( 'shortdesc' );
  		if ( $shortdesc ) {
  			$tagline = htmlspecialchars( $shortdesc, ENT_QUOTES );
  		} else {
  			$tagline = $this->determineTagline();
  		}

  		if ( $tagline !== '' ) {
  			// Apply language variant conversion
  			$langConv = $this->services
  				->getLanguageConverterFactory()
  				->getLanguageConverter( $this->services->getContentLanguage() );
  			$tagline = $langConv->convert( $tagline );
  		}

  		return $tagline;
  	}

  	/**
  	 * @inheritDoc
  	 */
  	public function getTemplateData(): array {
  		return [
  			'html-tagline' => $this->getTagline(),
  			'html-title-heading' => $this->titleData
  		];
  	}
  }
  ```

test "rank1376: taint returned through a component's own $this->getTagline() while a second class declares a method of the same name"
  lang php
  file includes/Components/Taglines.php
  reject VYQL-INJ-004
  code
  ```
  <?php

  namespace MediaWiki\Skins\Citizen\Components;

  use MediaWiki\Html\Html;

  class CitizenComponentPageFooter {

  	private function getTagline(): string {
  		return 'static';
  	}

  	public function getTemplateData(): array {
  		return [ 'html-footer-tagline' => $this->getTagline() ];
  	}
  }

  class CitizenComponentPageHeading {

  	private function getTagline(): string {
  		$shortdesc = $_GET['shortdesc'];
  		if ( $shortdesc ) {
  			$tagline = $shortdesc;
  		} else {
  			$tagline = '';
  		}
  		return $tagline;
  	}

  	public function renderHeading(): string {
  		return Html::rawElement( 'div', [ 'id' => 'siteSub' ], $this->getTagline() );
  	}
  }
  ```

test "rank1376: the same taint with the second class's method named differently"
